    "body": "I'd be willing to take a stab at this one. A question I had since it wasn't clear, if `truncate_to_repo=true`, should we still display the full repo name and use `truncate_length` after that?\r\n\r\nRight now, if I am in a path, `~/Projects/work/a_git_repo/packages/platform/src/modules/session`, it will truncate to `src/modules/session`. What if instead we did something like `a_git_repo/p/p/s/modules/session`?\r\n\r\nEdit: Or maybe that should be a different setting all together (`always_show_repo_name`) that should be in a separate issue.",
