    "created_at": "2019-08-25T00:44:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-25T00:44:28Z",
    "body": "I think `truncate_to_repo` should act purely as an override on `truncation_length` when using Fish-style truncation. The idea here is that anything that's not truncated would be the same, so Fish-style truncation only affects what happens to anything past `truncation_length` / the repo root. If you truly want to replicate Fish you can just set `truncation_length = 1` and turn off `truncate_to_repo`.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
